[N 29-30 Excavation Site: Wetlands]
[D Forever Druid 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Menethil pickups, the walk to Whelgar's dig site and a full run of the Excavation Site (Forever's new Wetlands five-man: Saltspine, Shadetooth, the Highland Horror and the Relic Guardian) with you as Cat Form damage, then the hand-ins at Rethiel, Whelgar and Menethil and the boat to Southshore.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 29-30|r  -  you step off the Auberdine boat at Menethil Harbor with chapters 20 and 21 behind you; hearth = Sentinel Hill and it STAYS there. This is the dungeon chapter for the Excavation Site, a NEW Forever five-man in the hills above Whelgar's dig site: about 17,700 quest XP handed in here at quest level (18,300 with the relic quest, 21,500 with the optional group quest Gleaning Our Future; the level-20 and level-24 quests pay less at your level), and 7,500 XP of quests picked up for chapters 24 and 25.
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r the DB has no creature rows, spawns or drop tables for this dungeon and there are no coordinates inside. Boss order and abilities come from Icy Veins, Method, kami-labs and a Wowhead-based article; drop rates from the item tooltips and kami-labs. All of it is |cffffcc00per those pages, unverified in game|r; where they disagree the line says so.
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Songblade Search (95772), Highland Hides (98815), Horrors in the Highland (95646), Gleaning Our Future (98310) if you took it.
[OC]|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r the run needs five: find a tank and a healer, plus two more damage dealers - you are melee damage in Cat Form (finder level 26; Method and the article also mention a meeting stone at the foot of the climb). The quests need 24, but the last boss is level 31 and Wowhead advises against entering at 24: you are well past that. Bring food, water and a repair.

[OC]|cffffffffMenethil Harbor|r  -  three pickups and a shopping stop, all within 8 units of the dock
At [TAR1480 Caitlin Grassman], [QT95737] [QA95647 Lost in the Thicket Things] (2,500 XP: her husband Ardin stands on a platform beside the last boss inside the Excavation Site; he is the hand-in and gives you Heartwoven for her) [G11.9,58.8 Wetlands]
At [TAR1217 Glorin Steelbrow], [QA322 Blessed Arm] (1,200 XP: the Crate of Lightforge Ingots goes to Grimand Elmore in Stormwind, chapter 25) [G10.6,60.6 Wetlands]
At [TAR2911 Archaeologist Flagongut], [QT942] [QA943 The Absent Minded Prospector] (2,400 XP: the Stone of Relu and Flagongut's Fossil, both on your way to the dungeon; hand in here after the run. 942 was a level-20 quest and pays little now) [G10.8,60.4 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Label (943):|r the fossil is one click beside Whelgar (|cff66ff66normal|r); the stone drops from the four raptor types of the valley and dig site and |cffffcc00the DB gives no rate|r - kill the ones you pass and take what comes; no stone after the run, skip the hand-in. The rewards (Relic Blade, Skullchipper, Archaeologist's Gown) are item-level 20: vendor all three
[O]|cffffcc00Food for the run:|r cook a stack of Mithril Head Trout (+20 attack power) if Cooking is 175, otherwise Succulent Pork Ribs / Longjaw; while the group forms, fish off the dock for more trout ([TAR3178 Stuart Fleming] at 8.0,58.4: Nightcrawlers) [G8.0,58.4 Wetlands]
[OC]Food and water from the general vendor [TAR1452 Gruham Rumdnul] (12.1,58.0), repairs at [TAR1450 Brahnmar] (11.5,59.9), then empty your bags

[OC]|cffffffffThe dig site|r  -  the road east and down into the valley, the same 3-minute walk as chapter 18. Raptors are level 22-29 and safe; the Goaz Warders (level 32 elites) look like statues that only wake with a Goaz Stone (chapter 18)
Follow the road east to the turn-off above the dig site [G34.1,40.8 Wetlands]
Kill [TAR1022 Mottled Scytheclaw] and [TAR1023 Mottled Razormaw] on the way down for the Stone of Relu (the Mottled Raptors and Screechers west of here drop it too) [G34.1,48.2 Wetlands]
Cook to 175: at your campfire by Whelgar's tents, cook Curiously Tasty Omelets until Cooking 175 - the Mottled raptors you kill on this walk and the Stone of Relu kills all drop Raptor Eggs (34-40% on Wowhead Forever: take what falls, no farming). At 175 the Recipe: Mithril Head Trout from chapter 9 opens (+20 attack power, you are 29-30) [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QA98313 For Further Study] (the Whelgar Relic Package goes to Historian Karnik in Ironforge, chapter 24; its XP is not in the DB) [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
Click Flagongut's Fossil lying beside Whelgar [QC943] [G38.9,52.2 Wetlands]
[OC]Prehistoric Prism (98824) is the follow-up to Lost Relic Carry (kami-labs and the article call it step 2 of 2, unverified), so Whelgar offers it after the run, below. If he already offers it now, take it and skip the later accept
Follow the track east and up to the dungeon door; Icy Veins puts it just south of the Thelgen Rock cavern and the DB at 47.8,56.2 [G47.8,56.2 Wetlands]

[OC]|cffffffffExcavation Site: Wetlands|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, finder level 26, ~20-35 minutes (Method), one outdoor map of four zones (Lost Marsh, Stalker's Thicket, Site of the Guardian, Lost Dig Site). Four bosses in a line: Saltspine, Shadetooth, the Highland Horror (a quest boss that drops no gear) and the Relic Guardian. Levels: Highland Horror 28 (the DB), Relic Guardian 31 (Method, Wowhead); no source gives the others. Nothing is picked up at the door
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Lost in the Thicket Things (95647) then Heartwoven (95809) - |cff66ff66normal|r: Ardin Grassman, on a platform beside the Relic Guardian, takes the first and hands you the Reed-woven Heart for the second
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Songblade Search (95772) then Fallen in the Fen (95795) - |cff66ff66normal|r: Daewyn Songblade lies in a camping hut just past Shadetooth (Icy Veins); the second goes to Dorin in Lakeshire, chapter 25
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Horrors in the Highland (95646) - |cff66ff66normal|r in one pass: the Highland Horror drops the Horrible Rootcore 64% of the time and it is a quest item, so each of you rolls your own; he stands at a camp hut after Shadetooth (Icy Veins)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Highland Hides (98815) - |cffffcc00grind risk|r: 4 Thicket Raptor Hides from Shadetooth and the Thicket Lurkers, Hunters and Matriarchs; the DB has no rates (kami-labs shows 5.5% on Shadetooth himself). Kill every Thicket pack you pass; with fewer than 4 at the end, abandon it [QS98815] - it is the smallest quest here (1,150 XP)
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Lost Relic Carry (95810, 630 XP) then Prehistoric Prism (98824, 3,150 XP) - |cffffcc00luck, 26.78%|r: the Titan Relic drops from the last boss only and the tooltip does not mark it a Quest Item, so expect a roll. Right-click it for 95810, hand it in at Whelgar and he offers the Prism, a carry to High Explorer Magellas in Ironforge (chapter 24). No relic on this run: skip both, the dungeon is not re-run for it, even though the Prism's druid pick is the best weapon on the route (Heavehammer, 2H mace 27.7 dps)

[OC]|cffffffffThe run|r  -  Saltspine first, on the crocolisk lake of the Lost Marsh. Young Riptooths come in threes with Fatal Bite (kill one at a time, no full AoE), Marsh Skulkers cast Muculent Rot (less Spirit and Stamina) and Skulkers and Elder Crocolisks use Tendon Rip, a 71% slow (Method)
[OC]|cffffcc00Saltspine|r patrols the lake edge: Dust Storm (-25% hit chance for anyone in melee range per Icy Veins; Method reads it as a threat cut - either way casters and ranged stay out of melee, and you, in melee, give the tank a few seconds before you open), Tendon Rip and Fatal Bite on the tank. Easy once the lake trash is dead; never pull him with a second pack
[OC]|cffffcc00Stalker's Thicket|r: Thicket Lurkers and Stalkers come in threes and hide invisibly in the tall grass until you step close - walk the path, not the grass. In Cat Form hit the tank's target from behind; if one of a three-pack runs to the healer and the tank cannot take it back, shift to Bear Form and Growl it. Thicket Hunters put Infected Wound (a disease) on the tank: cleanse it. Matriarchs and Lurkers apply Rend Flesh, a strong bleed
[OC]|cffffcc00Shadetooth|r (the hardest fight here per Icy Veins; patrols the raptor path with two Thicket Hunters): clear the raptors stealthed in the bushes and the crocodile den first, then kill the two Hunters before him (they can be crowd-controlled). His Terrifying Roar is an undispellable 5-second fear that runs you into the grass packs, so fight him with the group's backs to the cleared path. Rend hurts the tank; he enrages at 20% (Method) or 30% (Icy Veins) - stuns and slows. If the tank dies, shift to Bear Form and Growl. The article: pull him to the cove on the left after clearing it, the Hunters cannot swim
[OC]|cffffcc00After Shadetooth|r: Daewyn's hut comes right after him (Icy Veins) and the Highland Horror is the third boss, before the Relic Guardian (kami-labs, the article). Dragonmaw Saboteurs throw ground bombs (step out of the channel), Warders Mortal Strike and Net you (Blessing of Freedom breaks the net), Thaumaturgists come with a fire elemental: kill it first (Method; the sources do not say where they stand)
[OC]|cffffcc00Highland Horror|r (level 28 per the DB; Entangling Roots and Wild Regeneration per Method): the slimes around him are separate pulls, do not wake them early. Kill him fast and loot the Horrible Rootcore. The DB also pins a Highland Horror at 49.5,59.7 in the open Wetlands, just outside the door: if you ever see one out there, kill it there
[OC]|cffffcc00Relic Guardian|r (level 31, a construct that starts inactive): use the panel on his right (the Archival or Titan Control Panel) to start him. Thunderclap slows and cuts attack speed within ~10 yards, Arcing Smash cleaves the front (stay behind him - Shred wants it anyway), Knock Away drops the tank's threat (ease off until the tank has him back), War Stomp and a tank stun come now and then. He can be stunned, slowed and crowd-controlled (Method, Icy Veins)

Kill Saltspine on the Lost Marsh lake, then the Thicket packs and Shadetooth for four Thicket Raptor Hides [QC98815]
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Loot (Saltspine):|r roll on |cff66ff66Supple Bellyskin Leggings|r (leather legs +6 Str +14 Sta, 34.53% drop); |cff66ff66Glinteye Slippers|r (cloth feet +9 Sta +6 Spi, 30.95% drop)
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Loot (Shadetooth):|r roll on |cff66ff66Garb of Florid Feathers|r (leather chest +9 Agi +15 Int, 32.06% drop); |cff66ff66Raptor's Gaze|r (held in off-hand +4 Sta +4 Int, 33.52% drop)
At Daewyn Songblade's hut, [QT95772] [QA95795 Fallen in the Fen]
Kill the Highland Horror and loot the Horrible Rootcore [QC95646]
At [TAR262681 Ardin Grassman] on the platform beside the Relic Guardian, [QT95647] [QA95809 Heartwoven] (no spawn in the DB)
Start the Relic Guardian at the panel on his right and kill him (last boss)
[OC]Loot the Titan Relic from the Relic Guardian (26.78%) and right-click it: that starts Lost Relic Carry (95810), handed in at Whelgar below

[OC]|cffffffffAfter the run|r  -  the door is 20 units north of the Dun Algaz pass and 18 units south-west of Rethiel's clearing; everything below is one walk north-east to Rethiel, then west to Whelgar and Menethil
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r Gleaning Our Future: use the Goaz Stone beside [TAR271462 Golm], kill what wakes and loot the heart (level 32 ELITE, no HP in the DB; needs the other three hearts from chapter 19) - the whole group walks this detour together [QC98310,3] [G67.2,70.0 Wetlands]
Walk north-east up the valley to Rethiel's clearing at the road junction [G56.4,40.4 Wetlands]
At [TAR1244 Rethiel the Greenwarden], [QT95646] [G56.4,40.4 Wetlands]
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Gear:|r take |cff66ff66Ironwood Destroyer|r (2H mace 22.2 dps)
[O]At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QA95810 Lost Relic Carry] [QT95810] [QA98824 Prehistoric Prism] (only with the Titan Relic; the Prism's reward is picked at Magellas in chapter 24) [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
[O]At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QT98310] [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Gear:|r take |cff66ff66Golem War Cloak|r (cloak +6 Str)
[OC]|cffffffffMenethil hand-ins|r  -  walk back west along the road (about 3 minutes)
At [TAR2094 James Halloran], [QT98815] (1,150 XP, no item reward) [G8.6,55.7 Wetlands]
At [TAR1480 Caitlin Grassman], [QT95809] - take the Greater Healing Potion (in Cat Form your mana only pays for shifting and heals); the fixed Satchel of Potions is a trinket that gives a random potion on a 10-minute cooldown: wear it only if your trinket slot is empty [G11.9,58.8 Wetlands]
At [TAR2911 Archaeologist Flagongut], [QT943] [G10.8,60.4 Wetlands]
[OC][A Druid] |cffffcc00Gear:|r take |cff66ff66Relic Blade|r (dagger 10.0 dps +3 Sta)
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (943):|r the Relic Blade (10 dps) is an item-level-20 dagger: keep your weapon and vendor the reward


[OC]|cffffffffThe boat|r  -  in Forever the Auberdine boat carries on from Menethil to Southshore
Take the boat to Southshore from the Menethil dock (the sign on the pier names the destination) [G8.3,59.1 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r handed in here: Seeking Caitlin (95737), The Absent Minded Prospector (942, 943), Lost in the Thicket Things (95647), Songblade Search (95772), Horrors in the Highland (95646), Highland Hides (98815), Heartwoven (95809) and, if they came your way, Lost Relic Carry (95810) and Gleaning Our Future (98310). Carried on: Blessed Arm (322) and Fallen in the Fen (95795) for Stormwind and Lakeshire in chapter 25, For Further Study (98313) and, with the relic, Prehistoric Prism (98824) for Ironforge in chapter 24. Hearth = Sentinel Hill. Level 30 (Travel Form): Darnassus (chapter 20) if you were 30 there, otherwise the Stormwind Park in chapter 25 - no druid trainer in Ironforge. Next: Southshore
